Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Abstract", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bac14a37-852d-46a4-babf-a4e0a9f1364b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Lactase persistence is the textbook example of recent, strong selection in \
humans, and ancient DNA has turned its history into a quantitative time \
series: the derived allele tagged by ",
 StyleBox["rs4988235",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (the \[Minus]13910*T variant near ",
 StyleBox["LCT/MCM6",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ") is essentially absent in Mesolithic Europe, still rare in the Bronze Age, \
and reaches 50\[Dash]90% in parts of north-western Europe today. This \
notebook builds an end-to-end Wolfram Language pipeline on the public GLAD \
ancient genotype workbook (2,999 samples, 1,785 with a usable call, age, and \
location): it reproduces the regional rise with binomial logistic fits, \
embeds it in an explicitly spatial diffusion\[Dash]selection model on a \
European grid with a dairying-onset covariate, and fits that model with \
SMC-ABC \[LongDash] 400 particles, adaptive tolerances falling 0.245 \
\[RightArrow] 0.044 over five generations, 10,000 forward simulations. \
Posterior predictive coverage is 0.97; held-out-region and held-out-time \
validation and a five-scenario prior sensitivity analysis are reported \
alongside every point estimate. The posterior puts dairying-modulated \
selection at roughly 1\[Dash]2% per generation (95% interval \
0.001\[Dash]0.036) with northern regional multipliers above one \[LongDash] \
and, echoing Evershed et al. (2022), it cannot cleanly separate \
milk-use-modulated from uniform selection."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->14,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.98, 0.96, 0.9],ExpressionUUID->"34d2fb63-af17-47e1-8950-444a276e2a85"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Why lactase persistence", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5ecf5704-17d5-4719-bbd4-433fa9dc2375"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two facts make this system scientifically interesting rather than merely \
illustrative. First, direct ancient-DNA time series show the allele was still \
rare long after dairying became widespread: ",
 StyleBox["Evershed et al. (2022, Nature)",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " found that a selection model varying with prehistoric milk exploitation \
explains the allele trajectories ",
 StyleBox["no better",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " than uniform selection since the Neolithic \[LongDash] famine and pathogen \
exposure, not everyday milk drinking, are their preferred drivers. Second, \
the implied selection is very strong: ",
 StyleBox["Burger et al. (2020, Current Biology)",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " estimate a selection coefficient of about 0.06 for rs4988235-A over the \
last 3,000 years, starting from a Bronze Age frequency of only ~7%. A spatial \
model fitted honestly to the ancient genotypes should therefore (i) recover \
few-percent selection, (ii) show whether the data can tell dairying-modulated \
from uniform selection at all, and (iii) be loud about where its uncertainty \
lives."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"7de6b1aa-9e79-454d-847d-24f83007aa95"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. The data", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bac739f0-e3c0-4764-b9fa-dc9815c639c8"],

Cell["\<\
The input is the public GLAD ancient genotype workbook derived from the Allen \
Ancient DNA Resource v44.3 and used for the Evershed et al. (2022) analysis. \
The retrieval function downloads the workbook, records a SHA-256 checksum and \
a provenance manifest, and marks the raw file read-only. Everything below is \
reproducible from the repository with two wolframscript commands \
(\[Section]10).\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"34d61734-0d26-4c2f-ad9d-1db8254afc54"],

Cell["\<\
Get[FileNameJoin[{Directory[], \"src\", \"LactasePersistenceSpatial.wl\"}]];
raw = RetrieveRawData[Directory[]];
processed = WriteProcessedData[Directory[], raw];
samples = processed[\"CalledSamples\"];
Length[samples]\
\>", "Input",
 CellMargins->{{60, 30}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"67bef87a-48c5-455e-b2b3-acd1342f3ee7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Of 2,999 rows, ",
 StyleBox["1,785 samples",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " carry a genotype call at rs4988235 together with usable age and \
coordinates. Genotype strings are normalized so that A (and the \
strand-flipped T, which occurs in 3 heterozygous calls) count as derived and \
G/C as ancestral; single-letter pseudo-haploid calls contribute one called \
allele, diploid calls two. Coordinates reported in millidegrees are rescaled, \
and each sample is assigned to one of four coarse analysis regions echoing \
the published framing: British Isles (171 samples / 304 called alleles / 9 \
derived), Rhine\[Dash]Danube (341 / 591 / 16), Mediterranean (486 / 837 / \
28), Baltic (56 / 90 / 5). Two properties of these data discipline everything \
that follows: derived alleles are rare everywhere before ~4,000 BP, and \
sampling density collapses after ~2,500 BP, so any statement about the last \
two millennia is an extrapolation and is labelled as such."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"dbe77a27-0e0a-4466-b987-a0130e28695c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Reproducing the regional trajectories", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f44487d5-a54f-4919-aa81-b7cc37f41162"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before adding spatial structure, each region gets the standard non-spatial \
description: a binomial logistic trajectory ",
 StyleBox["logit p(t) = \[Alpha] + \[Beta] (10000 - t)/1000",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", fitted by direct maximization of the binomial log-likelihood over called \
alleles (no time binning enters the fit; bins are display only). Standard \
errors come from the numerical Hessian at the optimum, and the fitter flags \
any solution on a parameter bound \[LongDash] an earlier iteration of this \
project silently reported a boundary solution for the British Isles, which is \
exactly the failure mode the flag now catches."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"4aae337c-c6c2-4902-878f-70a00d35cfc2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
fits = FitAllRegionalLogistics[samples];
ExportRegionalFitOutputs[Directory[], samples, fits];
Dataset[fits]\
\>", "Input",
 CellMargins->{{60, 30}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"520bcd9d-5bb2-4a0b-ab19-ad55a7675209"],

Cell[BoxData[
 GraphicsBox[
  TagBox[RasterBox[CompressedData["
