Cell["\<\
Observed regional binned frequencies (points sized by called-allele count, \
95% Wilson intervals) with fitted binomial logistic trajectories. Slopes per \
millennium (\[PlusMinus]1 SE): British Isles 1.46 \[PlusMinus] 0.51, Rhine\
\[Dash]Danube 0.94 \[PlusMinus] 0.27, Mediterranean 0.86 \[PlusMinus] 0.16, \
Baltic 0.90 \[PlusMinus] 0.31. With a 28-year generation time these translate \
to approximate per-generation selection coefficients of 0.041, 0.026, 0.024, \
0.025 \[LongDash] the familiar few-percent picture, strongest in the \
north-west, compatible with Burger et al.'s 0.06 for the last 3,000 years.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"5f053969-a0f8-4dcb-8c3f-258056b9b4ac"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. The spatial model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3bd4fc02-ae98-4a32-9e9c-7ef022baef4b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Europe (35\[Dash]63\[Degree]N, 12\[Degree]W\[Dash]35\[Degree]E) is \
discretized into a 4\[Degree] grid of 84 cells. Each cell carries a regional \
dairying-onset time (Mediterranean 8200 BP, Rhine\[Dash]Danube 7600, British \
Isles 6100, Baltic 5600, other 6500) smoothed into a covariate ",
 StyleBox["D(t) = 1/(1 + exp((t - onset)/350))",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ". Local derived-allele frequency evolves in 250-year steps from 10,000 BP \
to the present:"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"6a05ff67-ae84-410d-8453-ec368c2f6f08"],

Cell["\<\
p[i, t+dt] = p[i, t] + g ( (s0 + sDairy D[i, t] m[region i]) p (1 - p)
                             + mig mean[ p[j, t] - p[i, t], j adjacent to i ] )

g = dt / 28   (generations per step)\
\>", "Program",
 CellMargins->{{60, 30}, {6, 6}},
 ShowStringCharacters->False,
 FontFamily->"Courier",
 FontSize->11,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.95, 0.96, 0.98],ExpressionUUID->"f31ff63d-5d76-4dbc-a276-35d9a2d664de"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with per-region selection multipliers ",
 StyleBox["m",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " and a small latitudinal/longitudinal gradient allowed in the initial \
condition. One forward simulation costs ~26 ms, which is what makes honest \
simulation-based inference affordable: the full analysis uses ~40,000 \
simulations in under 20 minutes on a laptop. The model keeps demography \
implicit \[LongDash] it is a reaction\[Dash]diffusion caricature whose job is \
to let the data say how much spatial structure, movement, and \
dairying-modulation they can actually constrain."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"09948362-a636-4404-9c8c-25a50681b13b"],

Cell["\<\
grid = BuildEuropeGrid[];
traj = SimulateSpatialTrajectory[
  <|\"InitialFrequency\" -> 0.003, \"SelectionBase\" -> 0.002,
    \"SelectionDairying\" -> 0.02, \"Migration\" -> 0.003|>, grid];
traj[\"TimesBP\"] // Length\
\>", "Input",
 CellMargins->{{60, 30}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"82f4e176-26b7-4221-b1e7-43155dfcfa20"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. SMC-ABC inference", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5db77e07-9f8a-479b-85da-40fd66fca95c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The likelihood is intractable in useful form, so the fit is \
simulation-based, comparing two families of summary statistics between data \
and simulation: (i) called-allele-weighted ",
 StyleBox["regional time-binned frequencies",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (39 bins), and (ii) ",
 StyleBox["spatial gradients",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " \[LongDash] because a spatial model fitted only to regional aggregates \
cannot identify migration, each sample is linked to its nearest grid cell and \
time step, and pooled north\[Dash]south and west\[Dash]east frequency \
contrasts over the last 4,000 years are computed identically for observed \
alleles and model expectations."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"04972d1e-c91f-4397-a4b6-9f3c7e6b134b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Inference is sequential Monte Carlo ABC: 400 particles, 5 generations, \
tolerance set each generation to the median of the previous population's \
distances, Gaussian perturbation kernels with twice the weighted component \
variance, importance weights ",
 StyleBox["w \[Proportional] prior / \[CapitalSigma] w K",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", and ESS tracking. One implementation detail worth flagging for anyone \
building something similar: with a 10-dimensional box prior, perturbing in \
the original coordinates wastes ~97% of proposals outside the box (0.7^10 \
\[TildeTilde] 0.03). The sampler therefore works in logit-transformed \
coordinates, where a uniform prior becomes an exact product of standard \
logistic densities, every proposal is automatically valid, and the prior \
density stays closed-form."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"4de44803-9124-4a58-a311-a69e6d5e3dde"],

Cell["\<\
smc = RunSMCABC[samples, grid, \"Particles\" -> 400, \"Generations\" -> 5,
  \"ProgressFunction\" -> Function[{g, eps, acc, ess},
    Print[\"generation \", g, \": epsilon \", eps, \", ESS \", ess]]];
draws = ResamplePosterior[smc, 100];
ExportSMCOutputs[Directory[], samples, grid, smc, draws];
Dataset[PosteriorParameterQuantiles[smc]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellMargins->{{60, 30}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"14fce47c-3c31-4fa0-9ebd-53899315fbca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Priors are uniform: ",
 StyleBox["log10 p0 \[Element] [-4.2, -1.5]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["s0 \[Element] [0, 0.015]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["sDairy \[Element] [0, 0.06]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " (spanning the published estimates), ",
 StyleBox["mig \[Element] [0, 0.015]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", regional multipliers within [0.4, 2.4]. The tolerance fell from 0.245 \
(prior median) to 0.044 over five generations and 10,000 simulations. The \
final effective sample size is 35 of 400 particles \[LongDash] \
importance-weight degeneracy is the known price of this weight formula when \
the posterior is much tighter than the prior, and it is reported rather than \
hidden; every interval below is a weighted quantile and should be read as \
approximate."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"c782e2b4-9f1e-45f9-95a8-1119b8af40c6"]
}, Open  ]],

