 TextAlignment->Center,ExpressionUUID->"b1b7cf8c-cb64-4aea-b3ed-d328e3f77713"],

Cell["\<\
Posterior predictive check over the 37 regional time bins: posterior draws \
\[RightArrow] forward simulation \[RightArrow] binomial sampling at each \
bin's allele count. Empirical 95% coverage is 0.97 (36/37). Bins with tiny \
allele counts (e.g. Baltic bins with n = 2) correctly produce near-full-range \
intervals rather than sharp wrong predictions.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"c11f5bdf-0ab2-4f75-a878-8d7e328bd1f5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Held-out regions.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Refitting with each region excluded and predicting its trajectory gives \
posterior-median RMSEs of 0.047 (Mediterranean), 0.065 (Rhine\[Dash]Danube), \
0.173 (Baltic), 0.180 (British Isles), with the 95% predictive intervals \
covering all held-out bins \[LongDash] wide where data are thin, rather than \
sharply wrong."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"2f1a6384-d486-404c-814a-55849a385632"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Held-out time.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " The most severe test: train only on samples older than 2,500 BP (1,543 \
samples) and predict the 7 most recent bins. The intervals still cover, but \
the median under-predicts the recent rise badly (RMSE 0.32). This is not a \
bug \[LongDash] it is the pipeline rediscovering, from deep-past data alone, \
that most of the evidence for strong late selection lives in the last three \
millennia, precisely the period Burger et al. (2020) analysed on independent \
grounds."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"ad4dc06e-d474-4ff9-b44e-792a92402def"],

Cell["\<\
cv = RunSMCCrossValidation[samples, grid];
timeSlice = RunTimeSliceValidation[samples, grid];
Dataset[cv]\
\>", "Input",
 CellMargins->{{60, 30}, {6, 6}},
 FontSize->11,ExpressionUUID->"83490dc1-b7ab-4e3c-9698-db890ea44fb5"]
}, Open  ]],

